# Scan output. Regenerated by `python3 inventory.py --workspace <name>` in
# under a minute, and it carries real subscription ids, resource names and
# workspace names -- tenant data, not source.
analysis.json
verdicts.json
__pycache__/
recommendations.json
report.html
detections.html
detections.pdf
telemetry_health_report.html
content_hub_recommendations.html
detection_recommendations.html
defender_plans.json
# Per-run diagnostic log, written by every verb since the CLI started installing
# the log handlers. It carries whatever a run logged -- workspace names and
# resource ids among it -- so it is tenant data on the same footing as
# analysis.json, and this repo publishes to a public mirror.
.pylon/
endpoints.json
rules_detail.json
templates.json
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# Resolved by `uv sync`, which every workflow runs unpinned (no --frozen or
# --locked), so nothing here or in CI reads this file -- it is a local artifact
# of running the tests. Committing it instead is a real choice: it would pin
# contributors and CI to one resolution, which is reproducibility bought with
# dependency drift nobody sees until the pin is bumped. Left untracked until
# that is decided rather than added as a side effect of a test run.
uv.lock

# Created by running the suite in a fresh clone.
.pytest_cache/

# Written by `coverage run`. A binary data file for one machine's run, not a
# report anyone reads from the repository.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# setuptools output. It was tracked, and it is a stale copy of src/ -- 29 files
# had already drifted from their originals, so a reader browsing the repo could
# land on either version of the same module. Nothing references it: not the
# packaging config, not the tests, not the release script, which builds its copy
# from `git archive HEAD src tests scripts ...`.
build/

# Generated run output. `design plan/detections/playbooks` write these wherever
# --out points, and the directory name is the operator's choice, so it cannot be
# listed. They carry a real workspace name and resource ids.
plan.json
report.json
detections.html
*-playbook.md
# The .kql files a run writes are named from the vector, so they cannot be
# listed either. Numbered prefix, technique, slugged name.
[0-9][0-9]-T[0-9]*.kql
